WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.540
Pipelines themselves require governance.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:16.120
Changes to pipeline configurations, automation scripts, deployment processes, secrets handling, approval rules, and security controls can affect the integrity of the delivery system.

3
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:25.920
Organizations should treat CI/CD infrastructure as an important system requiring documentation, review, testing, monitoring, and lifecycle management.

4
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.420
Pipeline-as-code practices can help make these changes visible and reviewable.

5
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.460
Pipeline changes should be traceable just like application changes.

6
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:41.360
Teams should be able to show what changed, who changed it, why it changed, how it was reviewed, and when it became effective.

7
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.800
This discipline protects both reliability and audit readiness.

8
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:52.780
If the pipeline is the mechanism that proves control activity, then changes to that mechanism must also be controlled.
